  "id": "pasat",
  "term": "PASAT",
  "definition": "PASAT is a standardized cognitive test used to measure how quickly and flexibly a person processes spoken information, along with mental calculation, sustained attention, and divided attention. In it, single digits are presented one at a time and the person adds each new digit to the one that came just before, with the score based on the number answered correctly.",
